A||||2||Krashdavus||Clutch release bearing symptoms??||||5||
Z||000000||Krashdavus||11-23-2001||12:45 PM||||I think the clutch release bearing is going in my vehicle.  I purchased back in May, it's on it's second clutch, but I don't know how many miles are on it.<P>Symptoms: Most noticible is the noise at idle in neutral that disappears when I depress the clutch.<P>Secondly, the clutch pedal SOMETIMES feels hard and it hangs up during mid stroke, like it's almost detented.  It also seems like I've lost some of the travel.  This detent feeling during depression is not evident with engine off.<P>Finally, the vehicle shudders as I engage the clutch pulling away from a stop. It doesn't shudder between gear changes..only in first-especially at low RPM engagement.<P>I just want to confirm I'm barking up the right tree.  I replaced the clutch cylinder piston this past summer to repair a leak.  It's been great up to now. <P>I'm looking at the RAM HD Kevlar clutch package (same as Fiero Store advertises).  Any good, or should I pony up to a Centerforce?  All comments welcome.  Thanks in advance.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Eriamjh||11-23-2001||01:28 PM||||I'm not certain, but I think the clutch release bearing is only actually in use when you depress the clutch.  Otherwise, it just sits on the clutch fork away from the pressure plate.<P>Engine shuddering when you engage 1st probably  means you just aren't giving it enough gas, but I don't know how you drive.<P>You may have a bad pressure plate.  Mine had broken fingers when I replaced it at 103K.  Put in a Centerforce Gold which was their cheapest model at the time.  It was nice and smooth and easy when does.<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||SLYGUY||11-23-2001||01:57 PM||||I'm having the same problem with my 104K mile 88GT. Throw out bearing makes noise whenever the clutch is engaged. Sounds like ball bearings rattling around. When I have the $$ soon I'm gonna have the clutch replaced as well as the pressure plate and throw out bearing. <BR>I'd bet that sound your hearing is indeed your throw out bearing. I've read accounts of this bearing being responsible for deteriorating shifting feel, as well as pressure plate damage.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Sly<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ViewImage.jpg"> ||||reg||1
